# Git — Commit Messages

When creating a commit, follow this rule — **not** ad-hoc styles from `git log` history.

## Commit workflow

When the user asks to **commit** (or commit and push):

1. **Message format** — use **this file only**. Do **not** run `git log` or infer style from existing commits (many are merge commits or legacy types).
2. **Inspect changes** — in parallel: `git status`, `git diff` (and `git diff --staged` if needed).
3. **Draft** — write subject (+ optional body) per the rules below; validate against [Validations](#validations).
4. **Commit** — stage relevant files, commit via HEREDOC, then `git status` to confirm.
5. **Push** — only when explicitly requested.

Format: [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)

```
<type>(<scope>): <brief description>
```

| Part | Rule |
|------|------|
| `<type>` | **Required.** One of: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`, `build`, `ci` |
| `<scope>` | **Optional.** Area affected — see [Scope glossary](#scope-glossary) |
| `<description>` | **Required.** Imperative mood, lowercase start, ≤ 72 characters, no trailing punctuation |

## Subject line rules

- **Imperative mood** — write as a command: `add`, `fix`, `remove`, `update` — not `added`, `fixes`, `removing`
- **Length** — keep the subject ≤ 72 characters (Git and GitHub truncate longer lines)
- **No trailing punctuation** — no period, exclamation mark, etc.

## Examples

```
feat(matchers): add #except_on option for Rails :except_on
fix(content_type): reject spoofed mime types without file magic
refactor(attachable): drop obsolete download_chunk Rails version check
test(validators): cover size equal_to boundary
docs(readme): document form_builder accept inference
chore(deps): bump marcel to 1.0
ci(gemfiles): pin sqlite3 >= 2.9 for Ruby 4.0
```

## Validations

Before committing, verify the subject line:

1. **Pattern** — `^(feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|test|chore|perf|build|ci)(\(.+\))?: .+$`
2. **Imperative, ≤ 72 chars, no trailing punctuation**
3. **Optional body** — blank line, then paragraphs with more context

## Body (optional)

Use when the *why* or trade-offs are not obvious from the subject:

```
fix(processable_file): reject SVG under libvips untrusted mode

Rails may set Vips.block_untrusted(true), which blocks SVG loaders.
Surface a clear validation error instead of a low-level Vips failure.
```

## Breaking changes

For incompatible API, schema, or behavior changes:

- Add `!` after the type/scope: `feat(rails)!: drop support for Rails < 7.0.1`, or
- Add a footer: `BREAKING CHANGE: infer_file_field_accept is enabled by default`

## Legacy types (do not use)

Older commits used non-standard types. Use these instead:

| Legacy | Use instead |
|--------|-------------|
| `refacto` | `refactor` |
| `dep` | `chore(deps)` |
| `lint` | `style` or `chore` |
| `new` / `add` / `adds` / `adding` | `feat` (or `docs` / `test` as appropriate) |

## PRs, merges, and Dependabot

- **Squash-merge PR titles** — must follow this format (the title becomes the commit subject)
- **Merge commits** from GitHub (`Merge pull request #…`) — leave as-is; do not rewrite
- **Dependabot bumps** — when squashing, prefer `chore(deps): bump <gem> from x to y`

## Scope glossary

| Scope | Area |
|-------|------|
| `attached` | `AttachedValidator` |
| `content_type` | `ContentTypeValidator` and spoofing checks |
| `size` | `SizeValidator` / total size |
| `dimension` | `DimensionValidator` |
| `duration` | `DurationValidator` |
| `aspect_ratio` | `AspectRatioValidator` |
| `pages` | PDF pages validator |
| `processable_file` | `ProcessableFileValidator` |
| `limit` | `LimitValidator` |
| `validators` | Shared validator behavior spanning several validators |
| `matchers` | RSpec/Minitest matchers (`lib/.../matchers/`) |
| `analyzer` | Media/metadata analyzers (`lib/.../analyzer/`) |
| `attachable` | `ASVAttachable` and attachable/blob loop |
| `analyzable` | `ASVAnalyzable` and metadata caching |
| `errorable` | `ASVErrorable` / error option shaping |
| `shared` | Other `ASV*` shared concerns |
| `form_builder` | HTML `accept` inference on `file_field` |
| `locales` | I18n files under `config/locales/` |
| `rails` | Rails version support / railtie / engine |
| `ruby` | Ruby version requirement or language-level changes |
| `gemfiles` | Bundler Gemfiles under `gemfiles/` |
| `dummy` | Combustion dummy app under `test/dummy/` |
| `tests` | Test suite (prefer a more specific scope when clear) |
| `deps` | Gem dependency updates |
| `ci` | GitHub Actions, lint/test pipeline |
| `readme` | `README.md` |
| `changelog` | `CHANGES.md` |
| `docs` | Upgrade guides and other docs under `docs/` |
| `agents` | `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/` |
